Wireless Router Hardening – Cisco Packet Tracer

This project demonstrates how I secured a home wireless router using Cisco Packet Tracer.

I hardened the router by changing default credentials, disabling remote management, configuring WPA2-AES encryption, separating Home and Guest networks, and verifying security through connectivity testing.

Tools used:
- Cisco Packet Tracer
- WPA2-Personal (AES)
- DHCP
- ICMP (Ping)

Key tasks:
- Secured wireless networks using WPA2 and AES
- Configured HomeNet and GuestNet
- Connected laptops securely
- Verified internet access
- Enforced guest isolation

This project helped me understand real-world wireless security best practices.

